<item>
            <title>[KYLIN-5555] Building model indexes on up-to-date segments will delete the indexes built on the out-of-date segments</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KYLIN-5555</link>
                <project id="12316121" key="KYLIN">Kylin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Currently, Kylin collects the out-of-date indexes from the up-to-date segments, rather than from all the effective segments, which will lead to the out-of-date indexes to be deleted. As a consequence, the query scanning on the historical segments will mismatch the indexes, to be pushed down to Spark engine directly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The issue is simply to be solved, please see the attached pic.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
